# Everything in this directory is a negative image of what you protect: the terms
# you designate as private, the names you have claimed but are not ready to
# publish, the files that stay in. That makes this the most sensitive directory
# in the installation and the one whose accidental publication would be worse
# than anything the gates catch.
#
# So the rule is deny-by-default rather than a list of filenames. A list has to
# be updated every time you add a file here, and the update that gets forgotten
# is the one that matters. Everything is ignored except this file, which is
# committed so the rule travels with the package.
#
# Keep it in place even if you move these files elsewhere. If you keep your
# dotfiles in version control, which is the case this exists for, deleting these
# two lines publishes the lot on your next commit.
*
!.gitignore
